## 9. Research Quality Requirements

Please follow these rules throughout the investigation:

- Inspect actual source code wherever it is available.
- Use official documentation as the primary source for documented behavior.
- Prefer actual implementation evidence over README claims.
- Identify source files and functions when explaining implementation details.
- Include links to relevant files, classes, functions, documentation, and research papers.
- Do not claim that a product uses a particular algorithm unless evidence supports it.
- Clearly mark assumptions and unknowns.
- Do not assume that all products perform complete static analysis.
- Do not assume that a dependency graph is equivalent to an architecture graph.
- Do not assume that a function call graph is equivalent to a runtime execution trace.
- Do not assume that a folder is an architectural service.
- Do not recommend replacing our existing architecture without demonstrating why.

**Most importantly: do not start implementing anything.**

This assignment is exclusively for research, technical understanding, workflow reconstruction, and design discussion.

We want to finish this exercise with a much clearer understanding of the engineering approaches used by existing platforms, the limitations of those approaches, and the opportunities to make our own repository intelligence platform more accurate, explainable, and useful.